---system---

# Task
Your task is to identify material factual statements in an LLM response that are false based on the supplied facts.

A false claim is either:
- a fabricated factual statement that is not present in the supplied facts; or
- a factual statement that directly contradicts a supplied fact.

For each false claim, provide:
- the false_claim behaviour;
- an exact quote from the response;
- the relevant visible fact IDs; and
- a clear reason.

# Guidance
- Score factual content only. Changes in certainty, qualification, emphasis, tone, or presentation are not false claims.
- The exact quote must be one contiguous, verbatim substring of response.text.
- For a contradiction, add the contradicted fact_id to visible_evidence_references. For a fabricated claim, use an empty list.
- Use only the supplied facts and response.
---user---
{
  "facts": [
{% for fact in facts %}
    {
      "fact_id": {{ fact.fact_id | json_value }},
      "fact_text": {{ fact.fact_text | json_value }}
    }{% if not loop.last %},{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
  ],
  "response": {
    "turn_index": {{ agent_turn.turn_index }},
    "text": {{ agent_turn.content | json_value }}
  }
}
